[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The render reads an export generated from the held graph

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SCRIBE-EXPORT-PAYLOAD
TITLE: The render reads an export generated from the held graph
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
A render obtains the export JSON from the held graph rather than by running a fresh export. StrictDoc's JSON generator is a pure function of a built index -- strictdoc's own server calls it against its live one -- so the daemon runs it against the resident graph into a directory the caller names, and every downstream consumer reads those bytes. The payload is written to a directory rather than returned, because the current export is about 10 MB. An export reconciles first, like any read.

Two things about those bytes differ deliberately from a hand-run export. First, StrictDoc's JSON generator drops ELEMENT and ID from element-grained File relations. `carry_file_element_into_json` patches that generator seam in memory so the daemon preserves both. Second, the generator receives each node's declaring document but omits its path. `carry_document_path_into_json` stamps every held document with its workspace-relative source path and patches `_write_requirement` once to emit `_DOCUMENT_PATH` on every node. Both patches are idempotent and fail closed when their upstream method changes shape. They live here rather than in the package because overlays/dev-tools/strictdoc.nix re-exports upstream's derivation unchanged for cache-hit parity; `strictdoc export` run by hand therefore still omits these additions.

The board adapter reads `_DOCUMENT_PATH` directly and no longer walks the canon for provenance. Other downstream readers continue to consume the same shape with additive metadata. The daemon's own graph load passes `skip_source_files=True`, so the source-traceability walk the project config enables does not run inside it and none of that walk's cost reaches a read.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Updated 2026-09-09: the daemon export carries File-relation ELEMENT and ID plus each node's workspace-relative `_DOCUMENT_PATH` through two in-memory, idempotent generator patches. The board consumes the path directly. The daemon's graph load remains exempt from the configured source-traceability walk.
<<<
